{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call-6e3fc51d-0ee7-4f27-bc55-1a05e1c154e4","type":"tool_result","content":"# prompt.yaml\n#\n# Fill this in BEFORE you start an AI session. The agent reads it first, so the\n# clearer it is, the fewer follow-up questions and the less rework.\n#\n# How to use it:\n#   1. Fill what you know. Delete the example lines (they start with \"e.g.\").\n#   2. Leave a field empty (\"\" or []) if it doesn't apply. Empty is fine.\n#   3. Short and concrete beats long and vague. One line per item.\n#\n# After the PR merges, CI resets this file back to the blank template, so every\n# new task starts clean. Don't keep history here, git already has it.\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# title: a few words, like a PR title. What would you call this task?\n# e.g. \"Show future hosted events on the host profile\"\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntitle: \"\"\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# type: pick ONE. It tells the agent which skill and checklist to follow.\n#   feature   new behaviour that didn't exist\n#   bug       something is broken (the agent fixes it, not just explains it)\n#   refactor  same behaviour, cleaner code\n#   perf      too slow, needs to be faster at production scale\n#   review    just look at the changes and report, don't edit\n#   question  explain how something works, don't edit\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\ntype: feature\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# apps: which parts of the repo this touches. Anything not listed stays untouched.\n#   server | web | crm | mobile | shared\n# e.g. [server, web]\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\napps: []\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------