{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call-ec526cfe-0194-42b4-8243-10b29654d64e","type":"tool_result","content":"# AGENTS.md — apps/web\n\nThe short, practical version of the rules for working inside `apps/web`. The root `AGENTS.md` is\nthe full rulebook (including the UI Guard) and wins if the two ever disagree.\n\n> **Read the root \"Absolute Rules\" first.** In short: never read a `.env*` file, and never run SQL\n> or any DB command. If you need an env value, or data from a database, ask the user.\n\nNext.js 16 (App Router) + React 19. The public site: event discovery, booking, accounts, the host\ndashboard, venues, plus the checker, door-staff, college-admin and admin areas. It is a PWA. CI\nbuilds it, but it is deployed outside the server stack.\n\n## UI Guard: ask before you change what people see\n\nAsk the user first if you are about to:\n\n- add a visible component, page, section or route\n- restyle anything (color, spacing, layout, type)\n- change user-facing copy, labels or the order of visible things\n- swap icons or imagery\n\nYou can go ahead without asking for: an obvious visual bug (broken layout, overflow), non-visual\nlogic inside an existing component (handlers, state, API calls), and import or type fixes after a\nrename. When unsure, ask. Ten seconds of asking beats an hour of rework.\n\n## Which skill to read first\n\n| You're about to…                                         | Read                                                  |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Build or restyle UI (only if the user asked for UI work) | `docs/skills/tunyt-web-design.md`                     |\n| Write page-level data fetching or a new query            | `docs/skills/tunyt-performance.md`                    |\n| Chase a bug or a failing spec                            | `docs/skills/tunyt-debugging.md`                      |\n| Touch auth, payments or sensitive data                   | `.claude/skills/security-testing-compliance/SKILL.md` |\n| Say \"done\"                                               | `docs/skills/tunyt-verification.md`                   |\n\n## Where things live\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── app/            # routes. Public pages, plus dashboard/, venues/, teams/, checker/,\n│                   # door-staff/, college-admin/, admin/, ...\n│   ├── api/        # thin Route Handlers that proxy to apps/server (see below)\n│   └── globals.css # Tailwind v4 tokens under @theme (there is NO tailwind.config.ts)\n├── components/     # grouped by feature: booking/, create-event/, dashboard/, team/, ui/, ...\n├── lib/            # redux/ (store, slices, api/*Api.ts), booking/, team/, razorpay/, utils\n├── hooks/\n├── sw/             # Serwist service worker, has its own tsconfig\n└── proxy.ts        # Next 16 proxy (the old \"middleware\"): CSRF gate + SEO URL casing\nunit/               # fast Playwright unit specs (no browser)\ne2e/                # Playwright end-to-end specs\n```\n\n## How the pieces fit\n\n- **API proxy.** `src/app/api/**` route handlers talk to the server through\n  `src/app/api/_lib/upstream.ts`, which resolves `API_URL ?? NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. Keep handlers\n  thin: forward, map errors, done.\n- **CSRF.** `src/proxy.ts` blocks authenticated mutations without a valid CSRF token. A new\n  `POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` route that can't send the header must be added to `CSRF_EXEMPT_PATHS`\n  with a comment saying why. Don't weaken the gate.\n- **Server state** goes through RTK Query. Each domain has an `src/lib/redux/api/<name>Api.ts`\n  that extends the shared `tunaiApi` (the name is legacy, don't rename it). **Client state** is a\n  Redux slice in `src/lib/redux/slices/` (`auth`, `ui`, `events`, `tickets`, `teams`, `booking`).\n- **Toasts:** `dispatch(addToast(...))` from `uiSlice`. Sonner is installed, but no `<Toaster />` is\n  mounted, so `toast()` imported from `sonner` silently shows nothing. Don't add new ones.\n- **Two UI toolkits live side by side, don't mix them.** Consumer pages use Tailwind +\n  `components/ui/primitives.tsx`. The host dashboard, college-admin, checker and door-staff screens\n  use `components/dashboard/tokens.ts` + `components/dashboard/kit/*`.\n- **Aliases:** `@/*` → `src/*`, `@icons/*` → `public/react-tsx/*`.\n- **Shared types** for events, tickets, booking and auth come from `@tunyt/shared`\n  (`packages/tunyt-shared`). Look there before you declare a new one.\n- **Reuse before you add.** Grep `src/components/` and `src/lib/` before writing a new helper or\n  running `pnpm add`. Ask before adding a dependency.\n\n## Rules that have bitten us\n\n- **Money on screen must match what the server charges.** Totals come from the same formula the\n  server uses: `computePricePreview` (`lib/booking/venue-pricing.ts`) and, for tickets,\n  `effectiveTicketPrice` / `hasTicketDiscount` from `@tunyt/shared`. Never show `ticketType.price`\n  or a bare `discountedPrice || price` as a total.\n- **\"N sold\" is a count of `SUCCESS` tickets**, never a stored counter.\n- **Price and quote UI:** skeleton only on the very first load. On refetches (stepper taps and so\n  on) dim the content in place so nothing flashes.\n- **Private event locations:** only city and state are public. Don't render the street address when\n  the location is hidden.\n- **`refetch()` from a hook that has `skip`** must be called behind the same condition. Calling it\n  on a query that never started throws and takes down the whole page.\n- **A Redux flag with readers but no dispatcher is a silent no-op.** Before you trust one, grep\n  for something that actually sets it.\n- **Tab bars and segmented controls** derived from `pathname` need a click-time optimistic state, or\n  they feel dead on a slow connection.\n- **Checker and door-staff requests carry their own Bearer token.** The shared RTK base query\n  must not overwrite that header or force-logout a host on a checker's 401.\n- **Cross-midnight venues:** \"today\" for slot booking is the *operating* day, use\n  `getEffectiveOperatingDate` (`lib/booking/venue-helpers.ts`), not `new Date()` truncation.\n- **`unstable_cache` keys must include the dynamic id** (`eventId`). Leaving it out leaks data\n  between events.\n- Per-user, JWT-gated data stays client-side. Don't move it into a server component.\n- **Rich text stored as Tiptap doc JSON** must be rendered as formatted HTML, never shown as raw\n  JSON or left blank, and its line breaks kept (`whitespace-pre-wrap` or real paragraphs).\n- **Share buttons share the event's short link,** not the full URL.\n- **`maps.app.goo.gl` short links** only give a plain 302 to a mobile user agent. A desktop Chrome\n  agent gets a JS page with no location. Fetch with the mobile agent first, and test against a real\n  short link before calling it done.\n\n## Checking UI work\n\n- Before changing CSS, inspect the real DOM and the current source to find the element actually\n  causing the problem.\n- Figma or screenshot work: compare the rendered page at phone, tablet and desktop widths against\n  the reference before claiming it matches.\n- Booking flows: run the Playwright coverage at small, medium and large viewports all the way\n  through payment and the success page.\n- Run `pnpm biome lint` before pushing and fix every warning, not just the errors.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\npnpm dev          # next dev (Turbopack)\npnpm build        # next build --webpack\npnpm lint         # biome check\npnpm typecheck    # tsc --noEmit for the app AND for src/sw\npnpm test:unit    # unit/ specs, no browser, fast\npnpm test:e2e     # e2e/ specs (needs apps/server running with ALLOW_DEV_OTP_BYPASS=true)\n```\n\nIf the app crashes with no code change after switching branches, delete `.next` and restart. Tests\nare Playwright only, never vitest or jest, and no new specs during a fix round unless the user asks.\nRunning e2e needs the API (and so the DB) up, so ask before you start it.\n\n## Before you say \"done\"\n\n1. `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` are clean (typecheck covers both tsconfigs).\n2. The matching unit or e2e spec passes if the change touches a booked flow.\n3. UI Guard respected, and the user approved anything visible.\n4. No `.env*` read, no DB command run.\n5. `graphify update .` from the repo root.\n6. Ask the user before committing.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8db18de0-e6fa-4cab-a756-dd1477016fa1","uuid":"d0f25691-cf3b-4ebd-8b0a-4d4621d25bdb","timestamp":"2026-11-20T17:33:23.663Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# AGENTS.md — apps/web\n\nThe short, practical version of the rules for working inside `apps/web`. The root `AGENTS.md` is\nthe full rulebook (including the UI Guard) and wins if the two ever disagree.\n\n> **Read the root \"Absolute Rules\" first.** In short: never read a `.env*` file, and never run SQL\n> or any DB command. If you need an env value, or data from a database, ask the user.\n\nNext.js 16 (App Router) + React 19. The public site: event discovery, booking, accounts, the host\ndashboard, venues, plus the checker, door-staff, college-admin and admin areas. It is a PWA. CI\nbuilds it, but it is deployed outside the server stack.\n\n## UI Guard: ask before you change what people see\n\nAsk the user first if you are about to:\n\n- add a visible component, page, section or route\n- restyle anything (color, spacing, layout, type)\n- change user-facing copy, labels or the order of visible things\n- swap icons or imagery\n\nYou can go ahead without asking for: an obvious visual bug (broken layout, overflow), non-visual\nlogic inside an existing component (handlers, state, API calls), and import or type fixes after a\nrename. When unsure, ask. Ten seconds of asking beats an hour of rework.\n\n## Which skill to read first\n\n| You're about to…                                         | Read                                                  |\n| ----------------