icit browser timezone).\n\nRules for your report:\n- Format each finding as: `file:line` + what is wrong + why it breaks + a concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output) + severity (high/medium/low).\n- Cap at 8 findings, ranked by severity.\n- Only report things you have VERIFIED by reading the actual code. Quote the relevant code line.\n- Skip generic best practices and anything you are not sure about. Do not report the same problem twice.\n- Prefer the highest-value bug you can point at with exact line numbers."}}],"model":"MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8db18de0-e6fa-4cab-a756-dd1477016fa1","uuid":"c51f93b3-65b3-4c0c-83d0-75962d147fbe","timestamp":"2026-11-20T17:34:09.190Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call-5470d650-ae5a-4bd0-a18f-ce45e4335c88":{"description":"Audit web booking funnel for bugs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are auditing the Tunyt event-ticketing booking flow in the web app for REAL, concrete bugs (not style opinions). This is a research-only task: do NOT edit any files.\n\nScope (read these files fully):\n- apps/web/src/app/venues/[venueId]/book/[resourceId]/BookingFunnelClient.tsx (4801 lines — read it in chunks)\n- apps/web/src/components/booking/BookingModal.tsx\n- apps/web/src/components/booking/steps/*.tsx (SelectStep, AttendeesStep, IdentifyStep, TeamSetupStep, ConfirmStep, PaymentStep, ReviewStep, ApprovalSubmittedStep)\n- apps/web/src/components/booking/BookingStepper.tsx, BookingSummary.tsx, HoldCountdown.tsx, FieldRow.tsx, SplitEditor.tsx, WaitingForTeammates.tsx\n- apps/web/src/lib/booking/*.ts\n\nHunt for these specific classes of defect:\n1. Double-submit / race conditions: a button that can be clicked twice while a mutation is in flight, creating two bookings or two payment orders. Look for missing `isLoading`/`isPending`/disabled guards on submit handlers.\n2. Stale state: a step that reads props/state captured before an async refetch; a quote/price shown that is not the one the server will charge.\n3. Error handling: a failed mutation that leaves the UI in a submitting state forever, or an error swallowed with no user-visible reason.\n4. Hold/expiry: the booking hold countdown expiring while the user is mid-flow, and what happens then.\n5. State reset bugs: navigating backwards/forwards between steps losing the user's selections, or a stale selected slot/time left over after the date changes.\n6. Off-by-one / wrong units: minutes vs hours, paise vs rupees, timezone handling (the repo rule: always carry timezoneOffsetMinutes, never rely on implicit browser timezone).\n\nRules for your report:\n- Format each finding as: `file:line` + what is wrong + why it breaks + a concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output) + severity (high/medium/low).\n- Cap at 8 findings, ranked by severity.\n- Only report things you have VERIFIED by reading the actual code. Quote the relevant code line.\n- Skip generic best practices and anything you are not sure about. Do not report the same problem twice.\n- Prefer the highest-value bug you can point at with exact line numbers."}}}
