{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_bf6874b6-63d2-4538-b919-1dd2c29fa249","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7804811d-daa0-4a1c-876c-2bdfd4a643ad","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit server booking service","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are auditing the Tunyt event-ticketing booking backend for REAL, concrete bugs (not style opinions). This is a research-only task: do NOT edit any files and do NOT run any DB command.\n\nScope (read these files fully, in apps/server/src):\n- services/booking.service.ts\n- controllers/booking.controller.ts\n- repositories/booking.repository.ts\n- services/ticket.service.ts (only the booking-confirm / availability parts)\n- routes/booking.routes.ts (or wherever the booking routes are defined)\n\nAlso look at apps/server/src/utils/ and any money/price computation helpers the booking service uses.\n\nHunt for these specific classes of defect:\n1. Money: integer paise vs rupees confusion; rounding at the wrong boundary; a total that does not equal the sum of its parts (the repo rule: money is integer paise internally, round only at the charge/payment boundary).\n2. Race conditions / overselling: availability checked and then written without a transaction or a conditional update, so two concurrent bookings can both take the last ticket. Check the Prisma transaction usage and whether availability decrements are atomic.\n3. Idempotency: a retried confirm / webhook can create two bookings or double-charge. Check for idempotency keys and status guards.\n4. Validation gaps: a status transition that isn't guarded (e.g. confirming an already-cancelled or already-confirmed booking), a negative quantity, a discount applied twice.\n5. Error handling: DB errors leaking raw to the client (the repo has a `wrapDatabaseOperation` helper that sanitizes them — check if new/other repo methods bypass it), or a failed write leaving inconsistent rows (no transaction).\n\nRules for your report:\n- Format each finding as: `file:line` + what is wrong + why it breaks + a concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output) + severity (high/medium/low).\n- Cap at 8 findings, ranked by severity.\n- Only report things you have VERIFIED by reading the actual code. Quote the relevant code line.\n- Skip generic best practices. Do not report the same problem twice."}}],"model":"MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8db18de0-e6fa-4cab-a756-dd1477016fa1","uuid":"0d4327fe-cd22-4d0d-9c28-029debf03eda","timestamp":"2026-11-20T17:34:14.787Z","wire_tool_inputs":{"call-7804811d-daa0-4a1c-876c-2bdfd4a643ad":{"description":"Audit server booking service","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are auditing the Tunyt event-ticketing booking backend for REAL, concrete bugs (not style opinions). This is a research-only task: do NOT edit any files and do NOT run any DB command.\n\nScope (read these files fully, in apps/server/src):\n- services/booking.service.ts\n- controllers/booking.controller.ts\n- repositories/booking.repository.ts\n- services/ticket.service.ts (only the booking-confirm / availability parts)\n- routes/booking.routes.ts (or wherever the booking routes are defined)\n\nAlso look at apps/server/src/utils/ and any money/price computation helpers the booking service uses.\n\nHunt for these specific classes of defect:\n1. Money: integer paise vs rupees confusion; rounding at the wrong boundary; a total that does not equal the sum of its parts (the repo rule: money is integer paise internally, round only at the charge/payment boundary).\n2. Race conditions / overselling: availability checked and then written without a transaction or a conditional update, so two concurrent bookings can both take the last ticket. Check the Prisma transaction usage and whether availability decrements are atomic.\n3. Idempotency: a retried confirm / webhook can create two bookings or double-charge. Check for idempotency keys and status guards.\n4. Validation gaps: a status transition that isn't guarded (e.g. confirming an already-cancelled or already-confirmed booking), a negative quantity, a discount applied twice.\n5. Error handling: DB errors leaking raw to the client (the repo has a `wrapDatabaseOperation` helper that sanitizes them — check if new/other repo methods bypass it), or a failed write leaving inconsistent rows (no transaction).\n\nRules for your report:\n- Format each finding as: `file:line` + what is wrong + why it breaks + a concrete failure scenario (inputs -> wrong output) + severity (high/medium/low).\n- Cap at 8 findings, ranked by severity.\n- Only report things you have VERIFIED by reading the actual code. Quote the relevant code line.\n- Skip generic best practices. Do not report the same problem twice."}}}
