{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a1fa06422a713bb0830e38","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * Money utilities — integer-paise arithmetic.\n3\t *\n4\t * Money is computed in INTEGER PAISE (1 rupee = 100 paise) to eliminate\n5\t * floating-point drift. Rupee `number`s only ever appear at the boundary\n6\t * (input from the DB/UI, output for storage/display). Rounding happens once,\n7\t * at the conversion to paise, because paise is the smallest unit money can\n8\t * actually move in (gateways settle in integer paise).\n9\t *\n10\t * Rules:\n11\t *  - Never do `a + b` / `a * pct` on rupee floats in money paths — convert to\n12\t *    paise first with toPaise(), compute with integers, convert back with\n13\t *    fromPaise() at the very end.\n14\t *  - Percentages stay as fractions (e.g. 0.025) and are applied to a paise\n15\t *    integer, then rounded to the nearest paise with roundPaise().\n16\t */\n17\t\n18\t/** Rupees (float) → integer paise. Single, deterministic rounding point. */\n19\texport function toPaise(rupees: number): number {\n20\t  return Math.round(rupees * 100);\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\t/** Integer paise → rupees (exact 2-dp value). */\n24\texport function fromPaise(paise: number): number {\n25\t  return paise / 100;\n26\t}\n27\t\n28\t/**\n29\t * Apply a fractional rate to a paise amount and round to the nearest paise.\n30\t * e.g. paiseTimesRate(90000, 0.025) === 2250  (₹900 × 2.5% = ₹22.50)\n31\t */\n32\texport function paiseTimesRate(paise: number, rate: number): number {\n33\t  return Math.round(paise * rate);\n34\t}\n35\t\n36\t/** Add two rupee floats via the paise grid (no float drift). */\n37\texport function addRupees(a: number, b: number): number {\n38\t  return fromPaise(toPaise(a) + toPaise(b));\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t/** Subtract two rupee floats via the paise grid (no float drift). */\n42\texport function subtractRupees(a: number, b: number): number {\n43\t  return fromPaise(toPaise(a) - toPaise(b));\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t/** Clamp a rupee float to ≥ 0 via the paise grid. */\n47\texport function clampNonNegativeRupees(n: number): number {\n48\t  return fromPaise(Math.max(toPaise(n), 0));\n49\t}\n50\t\n51\t/** Round a rupee float to 2 dp via the paise grid (legacy-compatible). */\n52\texport const round2 = (n: number): number => fromPaise(toPaise(n));\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"call-7804811d-daa0-4a1c-876c-2bdfd4a643ad","agent_id":"a6f93236d4c734935","session_id":"8db18de0-e6fa-4cab-a756-dd1477016fa1","uuid":"84d77c56-9b03-487d-8e14-bfddcb24d678","timestamp":"2026-11-20T17:34:38.410Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_01a1fa06422a713bb0830e38","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Audit server booking service"}
